      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should explain privilege to your 7-year-old in a way that's relatable to her everyday life, like this: \"Imagine you're playing with your friends in a big playground, and everyone gets to play on the swings and slide. But, let's say there's one kid who's really good at climbing and can get to the top of the jungle gym without even trying. That's kind of like what privilege is - it's when someone has an unfair advantage just because of who they are, like their skin color, where they come from, or what they look like. It's not because they're bad or mean, it's just that they have a different set of tools to help them succeed.\"",
